TEXT 56 128 Left 2 ;NOTE: Roff should be very high\nbecause of high R1
TEXT -8 328 Left 2 ;Small simulation timesteps\nfrom 500ms to 1000ms\nwith the breakpoint device
TEXT -88 -16 Left 2 ;Capacitive Paradoxon:\nIf we connect one loaded capacitance (c1) with E=500uJ  to another unloaded one (C2)\nhalve the energy is wasted in the resistance (E=250uJ) and the remaining energy\nin the both capacitances will be each 125uJ (sum=250uJ) after charging is off\nThat means that halfe the energy of the loaded capacitance is gone\nThis does'nt depend of the value of the resistance and is always the same\ntry it out with R=1/10=1e5 ohm
TEXT 104 168 Left 2 ;R1
TEXT 32 144 Left 2 ;C1
TEXT 184 144 Left 2 ;C2
TEXT 96 240 Left 2 ;Energy of capacitance C1\nE=C*U*U/2=100e-9*100*100/2=500uJ\nAfter (un)charging is off\nEC1=EC2=(C*U/2*U/2)/2=100e-9*50*50/2=125uJ\nsee also energy.wxmx in this directory
